.TH OCSFS\-DEFRAG 8 "March 2026" "ocsfs 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ocsfs\-defrag \- online defragmentation daemon for OCSFS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ocsfs\-defrag
[\fB\-b\fR \fIMB/s\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fIthreshold\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR]
[\fB\-1\fR]
.I mount\-point
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ocsfs\-defrag
scans a mounted OCSFS filesystem for fragmented files and
defragments them by copying data to new contiguous locations.
It uses the FIEMAP ioctl to detect fragmentation and the
OCSFS allocator's preallocation hints to ensure new allocations
are contiguous.
.PP
The daemon is bandwidth-limited to avoid impacting foreground
VM I/O workloads. Only one instance runs per mount point,
coordinated via a lock file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b " " \fIMB/s\fR
Bandwidth limit in megabytes per second (default: 50).
.TP
.BR \-t " " \fIthreshold\fR
Minimum number of extents to consider a file fragmented (default: 4).
.TP
.BR \-n
Dry run \- report fragmentation without defragmenting.
.TP
.BR \-v
Verbose output \- print per-file defragmentation details.
.TP
.BR \-d
Run as a background daemon.
.TP
.BR \-1
Single pass \- scan once and exit (no continuous monitoring).
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Pause defragmentation.
.TP
.B SIGUSR2
Resume defragmentation.
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Stop gracefully after current file.
.SH SYSTEMD INTEGRATION
A systemd template unit is provided:
.PP
.RS 4
systemctl enable ocsfs\-defrag@mnt\-pve\-fc\\\\x2dshared.service
.br
systemctl start ocsfs\-defrag@mnt\-pve\-fc\\\\x2dshared.service
.RE
.PP
Use
.BR systemd\-escape (1)
to convert mount paths:
.PP
.RS 4
systemd\-escape \-p /mnt/pve/fc\-shared
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkfs.ocsfs (8),
.BR ocsfs\-tool (8),
.BR mount.ocsfs (8)
